A||||6||murray||Dual Exhaust & 2.5L||||1||
Z||000000||murray||08-26-2001||10:08 PM||||My 87 Fiero SE 2.5 has dual exhaust & the real end is molded to accomodate this was this a factory option?||||reg||1
Z||000001||85SE||08-26-2001||10:30 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by murray:<BR><B>My 87 Fiero SE 2.5 has dual exhaust & the real end is molded to accomodate this was this a factory option?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hey Murray:<P>Yup, but pretty uncommon.  The dual exhaust with Aero package and 4 cylinder combination could be had on the 84 Indy (commonly accepted that about 2000 were made), the 86 4 cylinder SE (??) and the 87 SE (1400 made).  Most SE cars were ordered with the v6.  I personally love the look, especially the Indy Fieros.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I believe all 87 coupe bumpers were also "cut out" for dual exhaust, but that's different than your Aero package.  The coupe bumper just has around the bottom edge cut, as opposed to the obvious cutouts on yoru car.<P>Hope this helps!  Also, welcome to the Forum!<P>------------------<BR>Andrew Menchions - 85SE - AKA Fieroless in Newfoundland||||reg||14
Z||000002||Galen||08-26-2001||11:07 PM||||All 88 coupe bumpers not 87<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/sig.gif">   Ray -     <A HREF="mailto:galen@ezrpg.com">galen@ezrpg.com</A>     - <A HREF="http://www.fierolinks.f2s.com/" TARGET=_blank>www.FieroLinks.f2s.com</A> - AIM: GalenRPG - ICQ: 98668558||||reg||1
Z||000003||Kelvin Vivian||08-27-2001||01:47 AM||||ALL 1986 and 1987 SEs (both V6 and 4-cyls) have the quad pipe/dual exhaust from the factory. These SEs also have the aero front end, and side skirts.<P>In 1986 there were 4031 SEs with the 4-cyl duke.<BR>In 1987 there were 1401 SEs with the 4-cyl duke.<P>KV<BR>1987 SE 4-cyl, 5-spd<BR>1988 GT, T-top, 5-spd<P>||||reg||14
Z||000004||lowCG||08-27-2001||11:04 PM||||I had an '86 2.5 S/E,with the quad megaphone exhaust,luggage rack spoiler;never saw another one quite like it,all the other 2.5 S/Es seemed to have the standard exhaust.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Kelvin Vivian||08-28-2001||03:51 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by lowCG:<BR><B>I had an '86 2.5 S/E,with the quad megaphone exhaust,luggage rack spoiler;never saw another one quite like it,all the other 2.5 S/Es seemed to have the standard exhaust.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yeah,<P>In 1986 and 1987, most of the SEs had V6s.<BR>The 1987 SE 4-cyl I have now looks like it should kick some serious butt. Everyone thinks it has a V6 under it's decklid.<P>KV<BR>1987 SE 4-cyl, 5-spd, wing spoiler, sunroof, holley side scoop, quad megaphone exhaust, 15 in GT grey rims, burgundy/grey.<BR>1988 GT T-top, 5-spd<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||KnightRyder31||08-28-2001||11:39 AM||||Yup, my 86 SE has the "fake" dual exhaust also. At least it makes it look fast, thats about all it's going to do for you.<BR>||||reg||1
